course: dictionary
lesson: 16089
title: Wastage: what is lost or wasted
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wastage is a noun. It is the amount of something that is wasted or lost, and it can also mean the act of wasting. «The school weighed the leftover food to measure the wastage.» Here wastage is the food that nobody ate.
explain: Look at the word parts first. Waste means to use something badly, or to let it go to no good use. Wastage adds the idea of an amount: how much has been lost. When you see wastage, ask yourself: how much was wasted?
explain: Wastage often appears in science, maths and business. «Calculate the wastage.» is a maths instruction. It means work out the amount that was lost, for example when a piece of wood is cut and some of it is left as sawdust.
fact: Wastage means the amount of something that is wasted or lost.
fact: Wastage can also mean the act of wasting something.
fact: «Food wastage» means food that is thrown away or not eaten.
fact: «Water wastage» means water that is lost, for example from a dripping tap.
fact: «Calculate the wastage» means work out how much was lost.
exercise: «The school weighed the leftover food to measure the wastage.» What does wastage mean here? | The number of children who ate lunch | The price of a school lunch | *The amount of food that is wasted or lost | A kind of cooking pot
exercise: Ben says, «The wastage of water from that tap is wrong.» Which idea does wastage show here? | A tap that works very well | *The act of wasting water | A big swimming pool | Cold water in a glass
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to wastage? | *waste | saving | beauty | fullness
test: «Calculate the wastage.» In maths, what does this ask you to do? | Write the answer in words | Draw a picture of the sum | Round the number up to ten | *Work out the amount that was lost
test: Which is a good example of food wastage? | Eating every bite of your dinner | Sharing a packed lunch with a friend | *Throwing away half a sandwich that nobody ate | Putting leftovers in a box for tomorrow
exam: In a science report, «The wastage was 12 litres.» What does this tell you? | 12 litres were bought for the tap | *12 litres were lost or wasted | 12 litres were drunk by the class | 12 people wasted their time
